Subject: [PATCH] Prefer synchronized CPU copies for encoder staging

On POCO Pad X1, GPU writes into the private cached-coherent encoder staging
allocation produce corrupt encoded pictures without a kernel error. On the
same installed driver, selecting the existing synchronized CPU copy raises
the 30-frame H264 control from 16.194250 to 46.542374 dB PSNR.

Use the existing per-copier fallback already used by decoder exports. Keep
explicit diagnostic overrides, coherent allocation, DMA-BUF access/fence
handling, queue ownership and hardware encoding unchanged. This does not
claim a general kernel coherency fix or disable GPU copying globally.

Base: libva-v4l2 6d03c3f8fb19b86f84b2b6c60ff20d1402f0ac41 plus the seven
patches in signed uke-video-integration-1.0.0-1.fc46.
License: MIT, matching the modified upstream source.

--- a/src/encoder.cpp
+++ b/src/encoder.cpp
@@ -835,7 +835,7 @@
                 m->origin = MemoryOrigin::MsmCoherent;
                 e.staging[index] = m;
                 if (!e.copier)
-                    e.copier = std::make_unique<SurfaceCopier>(e.render_fd);
+                    e.copier = std::make_unique<SurfaceCopier>(e.render_fd, CopyDefault::Cpu);
             }
             e.copier->copy(e.staging[index], memory, e.width, e.height);
             memory = e.staging[index];
